      reply: `Here are some of the most famous and breathtaking waterfalls in Karnataka:

\u2022 Jog Falls (Shivamogga) \u2014 India's 2nd highest plunge waterfall (253m) formed by the Sharavathi River, cascading into Raja, Roarer, Rocket, and Rani.
\u2022 Abbey Falls (Madikeri, Coorg) \u2014 Nestled amidst fragrant coffee estates and spice plantations.
\u2022 Shivanasamudra Falls (Mandya) \u2014 Iconic twin cascades (Gaganachukki & Bharachukki) on the sacred Kaveri River.
\u2022 Hebbe Falls & Kalhatti Falls (Kemmangundi, Chikkamagaluru) \u2014 Spectacular cascades surrounded by lush greenery.
\u2022 Sathodi & Magod Falls (Yellapur, Uttara Kannada) \u2014 Secluded forest waterfalls in the Western Ghats.
\u2022 Iruppu Falls (South Coorg) \u2014 Sacred cascade at the base of the Brahmagiri wildlife range.

You can explore these and view distance from Bengaluru in our 'Explore Karnataka' section under Waterfalls!`,
